# Delegate All Work to Task Subagents

## Hard rule

The **main / parent agent MUST NOT** perform any task work itself.

This includes, but is not limited to:

- Reading files (`Read`)
- Searching code (`Grep`, `Glob`)
- Shell / git / network (`Shell`, `WebSearch`, `WebFetch`, MCP calls)
- Editing files (`Write`, `StrReplace`, `Delete`, `EditNotebook`)
- Linting, tests, builds, PRs, screenshots, computer use
- Investigation, planning deep-dives, verification, and follow-up fixes

**All** of the above MUST be done by creating one or more subagents with the **Task** tool.

The main agent may only:

1. Parse the user request
2. Choose subagent type(s) and model slug(s)
3. Call `Task` with a complete prompt
4. Relay / synthesize subagent results back to the user in 中文
5. Ask clarifying questions when requirements are truly blocked

Do **not** “just quickly” Read/Grep/Shell yourself. There is no exception for “small” or “one-line” checks.

## Model selection

When calling `Task`, set `model` to one of these slugs only:

```
claude-fable-5-thinking-high
claude-fable-5-thinking-xhigh
claude-opus-4-8-thinking-high
claude-opus-4-8-thinking-high-fast
claude-opus-5-thinking-high
claude-opus-5-thinking-high-fast
claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high
claude-sonnet-5-thinking-xhigh
composer-2.5
composer-2.5-fast
cursor-grok-4.5-high
cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast
gpt-5.5-high
gpt-5.5-high-fast
gpt-5.6-luna-high
gpt-5.6-luna-xhigh
gpt-5.6-sol-high
gpt-5.6-sol-high-fast
gpt-5.6-sol-xhigh
gpt-5.6-sol-xhigh-fast
